}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#ExponentialDistributionExpression",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Continuous probability distribution that describes the time between events in a Poisson process, i.e. a process in which events occur continuously and independently at a constant average rate"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Distribución de probabilidad continua que describe el tiempo entre eventos en un proceso de Poisson, es decir, un proceso en el que los eventos ocurren de forma continua e independiente a una tasa media constante"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Expresión para distribución de probabilidad Exponencial"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Expression for an Exponential probability distribution"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#ProbabilityDistributionExpression"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid363"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid364"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#ExpressionLanguage",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Language used to define an expression in a string. Generally used to compute something from other items of the model. Only the predefined languages are allowed, but future versions of the ontology may include more."
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Lenguaje usado para definir una expresión en una cadena de texto. En general se usa para calcular algo a partir de otros elementos del modelo. Solo se admiten los lenguajes predefinidos, pero futuras versiones de la ontología pueden incluir más."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Expression language"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Lenguaje de expresión"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid370"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#GuidelineCombinationMode"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid365"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#FailureOutcome",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "El fracaso de una estrategia. Es el resultado que genera failsIf (con el riesgo del parámetro, o cuando aparece la condición de salud) y al que sigue followedOnFailureBy en la forma abreviada."
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The failure of a strategy. It is the outcome generated by failsIf (with the risk of the parameter, or when the health condition appears) and followed by followedOnFailureBy in the short form."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Failure outcome"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Fracaso"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#TreatmentOutcome"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#SuccessOutcome"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#FirstOrderUncertaintyParameter",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Parameter whose value has first-order uncertainty, i.e., the value for each individual is not fixed"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Parámetro cuyo valor tiene incertidumbre de primer orden, es decir, el valor de cada individuo no es fijo"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "First-order uncertainty parameter"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Parámetro con incertidumbre de primer orden"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#ParameterNature"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid371"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#FollowUpCat",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#HealthCareCat"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#ResourceUsageCategoryScheme"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Follow-up"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Seguimiento"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#FollowUpStrategy",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A strategy related to the follow-up of a disease or condition. It may have treatment outcomes (TreatmentOutcome). A relapse after the response is modeled with a follow-up strategy: the success of a treatment is followed (followedOnSuccessBy, or the followedByStrategy of its SuccessOutcome) by a follow-up strategy whose failure (FailureOutcome) is the relapse. The risk of that failure is the probability of relapse among the patients who responded, and the failure may be followed by the treatment of the relapse (followedByStrategy). A long-term recurrence is not a relapse, but a new episode of the same acute manifestation."
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Una estrategia relacionada con el seguimiento de una enfermedad o condición. Puede tener resultados de tratamiento (TreatmentOutcome). Una recaída tras la respuesta se modela con una estrategia de seguimiento: el éxito de un tratamiento va seguido (followedOnSuccessBy, o el followedByStrategy de su SuccessOutcome) de una estrategia de seguimiento cuyo fracaso (FailureOutcome) es la recaída. El riesgo de ese fracaso es la probabilidad de recaída entre los pacientes que respondieron, y el fracaso puede ir seguido del tratamiento de la recaída (followedByStrategy). Una recurrencia a largo plazo no es una recaída, sino un nuevo episodio de la misma manifestación aguda."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Estrategia de seguimiento"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Follow-up strategy"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#Strategy"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid384"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid380"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#GammaDistributionExpression",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Continuous distribution of probability generally used to model costs, characterized by two parameters: the shape k (hasAlfaParameter) and the scale theta (hasThetaParameter), so that the mean is k * theta and the variance, k * theta^2. A gamma distribution expressed with a rate lambda (1 / theta) must be converted into its scale theta = 1 / lambda. In OSDi 1.2, the scale was called hasLambdaParameter."
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Distribución de probabilidad continua que se usa en general para modelar costes, caracterizada por dos parámetros: la forma k (hasAlfaParameter) y la escala theta (hasThetaParameter), de modo que la media es k * theta y la varianza, k * theta^2. Una distribución gamma expresada con una tasa lambda (1 / theta) debe convertirse a su escala theta = 1 / lambda. En OSDi 1.2, la escala se llamaba hasLambdaParameter."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Expresión para distribución de probabilidad Gamma"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Expression for a Gamma probability distribution"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#ProbabilityDistributionExpression"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid385"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid386"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid387"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#Group",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A group of model items. Useful to categorize or 'putting together' manifestations (e.g. all the eye-related manifestations of diabetes) or other model items"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Un grupo de elementos del modelo. Útil para clasificar o «agrupar» manifestaciones (p. ej., todas las manifestaciones oculares de la diabetes) u otros elementos del modelo"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Group"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Grupo"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#ModelItem"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid388"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#GroupableModelItem",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A model item that can be put in a group"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Un elemento del modelo que puede incluirse en un grupo"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Elemento del modelo agrupable"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Groupable model item"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#ModelItem"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid392"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#GroupableModelItemWithProportion",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A groupable model item that declares its proportion within the group (hasProportionWithinGroup)"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Un elemento del modelo agrupable que declara su proporción dentro del grupo (hasProportionWithinGroup)"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Elemento del modelo agrupable con proporción"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Groupable model item with proportion"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#GroupableModelItem"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid396"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/ontologies-ULL/OSDi#Guideline",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "La forma en que se aplica una tecnología sanitaria o una estrategia: qué dosis, con qué frecuencia (aplicaciones por periodo), durante cuánto tiempo (duración o número de aplicaciones), cuándo empieza (desfase) y a quién (límites de edad, expresiones de condición). Una pauta puede descomponerse en subpautas, de forma recursiva."
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The way a health technology or strategy is applied: what dose, how often (frequency per period), for how long (duration or number of applications), when it starts (offset) and to whom (age bounds, condition expressions). A guideline may be decomposed into sub-guidelines, recursively."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Guideline"
  }, {
    "@language" : "es",
    "@value" : "Pauta"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
